# Build context for every Dockerfile in the repository (apps/*/Dockerfile and
# docker/*/Dockerfile all build from the root, because the workspace is one install).
# What is left out: dependencies and build output (installed and built inside the image),
# every environment file but the template, the tests and their output, tooling caches,
# the docs and screenshots, and the git history.
#
# Nothing shipped may import an excluded path: a source file that does builds on a full
# checkout and fails inside the image, which is how the public `/docs` page's contract
# fixtures once reached a deploy (docs/decisions.md). They now live in
# `apps/purse/src/docs/contract-fixtures.json`. `test/docker.test.ts` fails if shipped
# source reaches into `test/`, `e2e/` or `docs/` again, and CI builds every image.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test
**/e2e
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/.vitest
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
docs
docker/postgres
.lavish
.claude
.railway
.agents
*.md
!README.md
.DS_Store
